    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "June\nTwenty-seventh,\n19 2 7.\nSupervisor Milo F. Kent,\nChairman Airport Committee,\nBoard of Supervisors,\nCity and County\nof San Francisco,\nCity Hall, San Francisco.\nDear Sir:\nAt the time the San Francisco Chamber of Commerce recommended\nto the supervisors the establishment of meteorological stations at the\ncontemplated airport sites, they also recommended that this work snoud\nbe supplemented by actual flying conditions.\nAt that time I discussed the matter with Major Clagett,\nCommanding Officer of the Ninth Corps Division.\nHe informed me\nthat\nthe Government would be glad to cooperate, but that they had a very\n1imited amount of gasoline allotted for their work, and it the city\nwould supply the necessary gasoline the Government would furnish the\nplane and pilot and would be pleased to make the necessary observations.\nThe cost of this work would be from $1,000. to $1,500. fox\nthe period of one year, making flights over all the contemplated fields\ntwo to three times a week. I discussed this matter with Major Clagett\nagain about a week ago, and he stated that the proposition was still\nopen.\nAs we commence our meteorological examinations on the Ist of\nJuly, it seems to me to be advisable that the flying tests should cover\nthe same period.\nI would be pleased to take up this matter with Major Clagett\nIf the Committee so desires, or your Committee can attend to the\nmatter directly.\nVery truly yours,\nRIGHT OF WAY AGENT.\nJJP: KH"
